<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>2026-2027 English Annual Plan – Grade 8</title><style>@page{size:A4 landscape;margin:.45in}body{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#111;font-size:9pt}h1{text-align:center;font-size:16pt;margin:4px}h2{font-size:11pt}.meta,.themes,.plan,.sign{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}.meta td,.themes th,.themes td,.plan th,.plan td,.sign td{border:1px solid #555;padding:4px;vertical-align:top}.themes th,.plan th{background:#dceaf4;text-align:center}.themes td{font-size:7.5pt}.plan{table-layout:fixed}.plan th{font-size:6.5pt}.plan td{font-size:6.3pt;line-height:1.12}.plan th:nth-child(1){width:7%}.plan th:nth-child(2){width:4%}.plan th:nth-child(3){width:14%}.plan th:nth-child(4){width:19%}.plan th:nth-child(5){width:18%}.plan th:nth-child(6){width:13%}.plan th:nth-child(7){width:12%}.plan th:nth-child(8){width:13%}.note{font-size:8pt}.sign td{height:55px;text-align:center}</style></head><body><div style="text-align:center;font-weight:bold">T.C.<br>MINISTRY OF NATIONAL EDUCATION</div><h1>2026–2027 ENGLISH LANGUAGE COURSE ANNUAL PLAN — GRADE 8</h1><table class="meta"><tr><td><b>School</b><br>____________________</td><td><b>Teacher</b><br>____________________</td><td><b>Grade</b><br>8</td><td><b>Weekly Hours</b><br>4</td><td><b>Programme</b><br>Current English programme for 2026–2027</td><td><b>Academic Year</b><br>2026–2027</td></tr></table><p class="note"><b>Basis:</b> MEB 2026–2027 working calendar and the applicable English Language Curriculum. Original DijiMedu working document. Review against the current textbook, school/subject-group decisions, BEP provisions and local school planning before approval.</p><h2>THEME / UNIT DISTRIBUTION</h2><table class="themes"><tr><th>No.</th><th>Theme / Unit</th><th>Content Framework</th><th>Indicative Learning Focus</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td><b>Unit 1 – Friendship</b></td><td>Friendship, personal qualities, preferences, accepting and refusing invitations</td><td>Integrated language skills and communication</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><b>Unit 2 – Teen Life</b></td><td>Teen routines, preferences, activities, likes, dislikes and daily communication</td><td>Integrated language skills and communication</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><b>Unit 3 – In the Kitchen</b></td><td>Recipes, food preparation, ingredients, sequencing and instructions</td><td>Integrated language skills and communication</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><b>Unit 4 – On the Phone</b></td><td>Telephone conversations, requests, messages, appointments and communication</td><td>Integrated language skills and communication</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><b>Unit 5 – The Internet</b></td><td>Internet use, digital communication, online habits and safety</td><td>Integrated language skills and communication</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><b>Unit 6 – Adventures</b></td><td>Experiences, past events, travel, activities and storytelling</td><td>Integrated language skills and communication</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><b>Unit 7 – Tourism</b></td><td>Tourism, travel, destinations, cultural places and directions</td><td>Integrated language skills and communication</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><b>Unit 8 – Chores</b></td><td>Household chores, duties, responsibilities and cooperation</td><td>Integrated language skills and communication</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td><b>Unit 9 – Science</b></td><td>Science, inventions, experiments, discoveries and scientific communication</td><td>Integrated language skills and communication</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td><b>Unit 10 – Natural Forces</b></td><td>Natural forces, disasters, safety, preparedness and responsible action</td><td>Integrated language skills and communication</td></tr></table><h2>WEEKLY ANNUAL PLAN</h2><table class="plan"><thead><tr><th>WEEK / DATES</th><th>HOURS</th><th>THEME / UNIT &amp; CONTENT</th><th>LEARNING OUTCOMES &amp; PROCESS COMPONENTS</th><th>LEARNING–TEACHING EXPERIENCES</th><th>DIFFERENTIATION</th><th>ASSESSMENT &amp; EVALUATION</th><th>IMPORTANT DAYS / SCHOOL-BASED PLANNING</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Week 1<br>14 Sept 2026 –<br>18 Sept 2026</td><td>4</td><td><b>Unit 1 – Friendship</b><br>Friendship, personal qualities, preferences, accepting and refusing invitations</td><td>Integrated listening, speaking, reading and writing; target vocabulary and language functions; guided production, communication and consolidation.</td><td>Activate prior knowledge; introduce contextual input; model target language and vocabulary. Pair/group work, role-play, picture or text-based tasks, short performance/product and age-appropriate digital or visual materials.</td><td>Support: visuals, word banks, sentence frames, modelling, repetition and peer support.<br>Enrichment: extended speaking/writing, choice tasks or mini-project.</td><td>Observation checklist, questioning, exit task, short performance/product, self-assessment and teacher feedback.</td><td>School opening / orientation</td></tr><tr><td>Week 2<br>21 Sept 2026 –<br>25 Sept 2026</td><td>4</td><td><b>Unit 1 – Friendship</b><br>Friendship, personal qualities, preferences, accepting and refusing invitations</td><td>Integrated listening, speaking, reading and writing; target vocabulary and language functions; guided production, communication and consolidation.</td><td>Activate prior knowledge; introduce contextual input; model target language and vocabulary. Pair/group work, role-play, picture or text-based tasks, short performance/product and age-appropriate digital or visual materials.</td><td>Support: visuals, word banks, sentence frames, modelling, repetition and peer support.<br>Enrichment: extended speaking/writing, choice tasks or mini-project.</td><td>Observation checklist, questioning, exit task, short performance/product, self-assessment and teacher feedback.</td><td>School-based planning as required</td></tr><tr><td>Week 3<br>28 Sept 2026 –<br>02 Oct 2026</td><td>4</td><td><b>Unit 1 – Friendship</b><br>Friendship, personal qualities, preferences, accepting and refusing invitations</td><td>Integrated listening, speaking, reading and writing; target vocabulary and language functions; guided production, communication and consolidation.</td><td>Practise comprehension and production through contextual, collaborative tasks. Pair/group work, role-play, picture or text-based tasks, short performance/product and age-appropriate digital or visual materials.</td><td>Support: visuals, word banks, sentence frames, modelling, repetition and peer support.<br>Enrichment: extended speaking/writing, choice tasks or mini-project.</td><td>Observation checklist, questioning, exit task, short performance/product, self-assessment and teacher feedback.</td><td>School-based planning as required</td></tr><tr><td>Week 4<br>05 Oct 2026 –<br>09 Oct 2026</td><td>4</td><td><b>Unit 2 – Teen Life</b><br>Teen routines, preferences, activities, likes, dislikes and daily communication</td><td>Integrated listening, speaking, reading and writing; target vocabulary and language functions; guided production, communication and consolidation.</td><td>Consolidate through integrated practice; communicate; reflect and revise. Pair/group work, role-play, picture or text-based tasks, short performance/product and age-appropriate digital or visual materials.</td><td>Support: visuals, word banks, sentence frames, modelling, repetition and peer support.<br>Enrichment: extended speaking/writing, choice tasks or mini-project.</td><td>Observation checklist, questioning, exit task, short performance/product, self-assessment and teacher feedback.</td><td>School-based planning as required</td></tr><tr><td>Week 5<br>12 Oct 2026 –<br>16 Oct 2026</td><td>4</td><td><b>Unit 2 – Teen Life</b><br>Teen routines, preferences, activities, likes, dislikes and daily communication</td><td>Integrated listening, speaking, reading and writing; target vocabulary and language functions; guided production, communication and consolidation.</td><td>Practise comprehension and production throu